meta {
  name: Update Master Profile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/me
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "category_ids": [{{category_id}}],
    "experience_years": 8,
    "about": "Сантехник с 2017 года. Установка смесителей, замена труб, устранение протечек."
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Master Profile

  The master edits their own trade details. Every field is `sometimes` — send
  only what changed, the rest is left alone. Changing the categories does **not**
  send the master back to review: they keep working, the administrator simply
  sees the new data in the panel.

  Name, phone and **city** are not here — they live on the client account and
  are edited in `03_profile` → Update Profile; the master profile is kept in
  sync from there automatically, so a person has one name and one city.

  **Fields:**

  | Field              | Rules                                                              |
  |--------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `category_ids`     | optional, 1..10 distinct ids, **subcategories only** (`parent_id` not null) |
  | `experience_years` | optional, integer 0..70                                             |
  | `about`            | optional, nullable, up to 1000 chars — send `null` to clear it      |

  `category_ids` replaces the whole list (it is a sync, not an append). An empty
  array is rejected: a master with no category drops out of the auto-search feed.
  Omit the key entirely to keep the current categories.

  Root categories are rejected on purpose — they are headings in the catalog,
  not trades. Take the ids from `children[]` in `02_catalog` → List Categories.

  **Partial update — just the experience:**
  ```json
  { "experience_years": 12 }
  ```

  **Clearing the "about" text:**
  ```json
  { "about": null }
  ```

  **Response 200:** `MasterProfileResource` — the same shape as Get My Profile.
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Aydogdy Ussadow",
      "phone": "+99362111222",
      "is_active": true,
      "is_available": true,
      "access_expires_at": "2026-12-31",
      "experience_years": 8,
      "about": "Сантехник с 2017 года. Установка смесителей, замена труб, устранение протечек.",
      "city": { "id": 5, "name": "Ашхабад" },
      "categories": [{ "id": 2, "name": "Сантехника" }]
    }
  }
  ```

  **Errors:**
  - `401` — missing / invalid token
  - `403` — token has no usable master profile (see `reason` in the collection
    docs); an applicant under review or a lapsed subscription cannot edit
  - `422` — validation error; `message` repeats the first error, `errors` carries
    them all:
    ```json
    {
      "message": "Выбранное значение для category_ids.0 не найдено.",
      "errors": {
        "category_ids.0": ["Выбранное значение для category_ids.0 не найдено."]
      }
    }
    ```

  **Not writable here** — ignored even if sent: `status`, `is_active`,
  `is_available` (use Set Availability), `access_expires_at`, `name`, `phone`,
  `city_id` (use `03_profile` → Update Profile).
}
